{"timestamp": "2026-05-12T09:36:57.310802", "model": "deepseek-coder:6.7b-instruct", "task_id": "math_005_4", "base_task_id": "math_005", "category_id": "4", "difficulty": "easy", "source_task_id": "5", "source_old_id": "vietjack_math_v5_0005", "passed": false, "values_passed": 0, "values_total": 1, "expected_answer": 3.0, "extracted_values": [11.0], "errors": ["Expected 3.0, got 11.0"], "duration_seconds": 2.9912071228027344, "prompt_tokens": 89, "completion_tokens": 146, "response_text": "Here is a Python program that computes the value of \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{99}}{\\sqrt{11}}\\) using the math library's sqrt function:\n\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Compute square roots\nsqrt_99 = math.sqrt(99)\nsqrt_11 = math.sqrt(11)\n\n# Divide them\nresult = sqrt_99 / sqrt_11\nprint(result)\n```\nThis program first computes the square root of 99 and 11, then divides the result of the latter by the former to get the final result. The print statement outputs this result.\n"}
