{"timestamp": "2026-05-12T09:37:45.740582", "model": "deepseek-coder:6.7b-instruct", "task_id": "math_006_1", "base_task_id": "math_006", "category_id": "1", "difficulty": "medium", "source_task_id": "6", "source_old_id": "vietjack_math_v5_0006", "passed": false, "values_passed": 0, "values_total": 1, "expected_answer": 0.22330097087378642, "extracted_values": [], "errors": ["Expected 1 numeric value(s), extracted 0: []"], "duration_seconds": 3.8868627548217773, "prompt_tokens": 107, "completion_tokens": 194, "response_text": "Here is a Python program to solve this problem using basic principles of statistics:\n\n```python\n# define the number of each color of balls\nred_balls = 13\nyellow_balls = 10\nwhite_balls = 80\n\n# calculate total number of balls\ntotal_balls = red_balls + yellow_balls + white_balls\n\n# calculate probability that the drawn ball is not white\nprobability_not_white = 1 - (white_balls / total_balls)\n\nprint(\"The probability that the drawn ball is not white is:\", probability_not_white)\n```\nThis program first calculates the total number of balls by adding up the numbers of each color. It then subtracts the probability of drawing a white ball from 1 to find the probability of drawing any other color. The result is printed out at the end.\n"}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-12T09:37:47.990748", "model": "deepseek-coder:6.7b-instruct", "task_id": "math_006_2", "base_task_id": "math_006", "category_id": "2", "difficulty": "medium", "source_task_id": "6", "source_old_id": "vietjack_math_v5_0006", "passed": false, "values_passed": 0, "values_total": 1, "expected_answer": 0.22330097087378642, "extracted_values": [0.187], "errors": ["Expected 0.22330097087378642, got 0.187"], "duration_seconds": 2.248349189758301, "prompt_tokens": 122, "completion_tokens": 105, "response_text": "The total number of balls in the box is 13 + 10 (red + yellow) + 80 (white). So there are 123 balls in total.\n\nThe number of non-white balls is 13 (red) + 10 (yellow), so there are 23 non-white balls.\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly drawn ball is not white is 23 out of 123 or approximately 0.187.\n"}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-12T09:37:49.834737", "model": "deepseek-coder:6.7b-instruct", "task_id": "math_006_3", "base_task_id": "math_006", "category_id": "3", "difficulty": "medium", "source_task_id": "6", "source_old_id": "vietjack_math_v5_0006", "passed": false, "values_passed": 0, "values_total": 1, "expected_answer": 0.22330097087378642, "extracted_values": [0.22456], "errors": ["Expected 0.22330097087378642, got 0.22456"], "duration_seconds": 1.8422963619232178, "prompt_tokens": 135, "completion_tokens": 83, "response_text": "The total number of balls in the box is 13 + 10 + 80 = 103. The number of non-white balls is 13 + 10 = 23. Therefore, the probability that a randomly drawn ball is not white is 23 out of 103 or approximately 0.22456 (rounded to four decimal places).\n"}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-12T09:37:53.784114", "model": "deepseek-coder:6.7b-instruct", "task_id": "math_006_4", "base_task_id": "math_006", "category_id": "4", "difficulty": "medium", "source_task_id": "6", "source_old_id": "vietjack_math_v5_0006", "passed": false, "values_passed": 0, "values_total": 1, "expected_answer": 0.22330097087378642, "extracted_values": [], "errors": ["Expected 1 numeric value(s), extracted 0: []"], "duration_seconds": 3.9481570720672607, "prompt_tokens": 112, "completion_tokens": 197, "response_text": "Here's a Python program to solve this problem using basic probability theory:\n\n```python\n# define the total number of balls in the box\ntotal_balls = 13 + 10 + 80  # red + yellow + white\n\n# calculate the number of non-white balls\nnon_white_balls = total_balls - 80  # subtract the number of white balls from total\n\n# calculate the probability that a ball drawn at random is not white\nprobability = non_white_balls / total_balls\n\nprint(\"The probability that the drawn ball is not white is\", probability)\n```\nThis program first calculates the total number of balls in the box, then subtracts the number of white balls to find the number of other balls. It then divides this by the total number of balls to get the probability. The result is printed out at the end.\n"}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-12T09:37:55.960338", "model": "deepseek-coder:6.7b-instruct", "task_id": "math_006_5", "base_task_id": "math_006", "category_id": "5", "difficulty": "medium", "source_task_id": "6", "source_old_id": "vietjack_math_v5_0006", "passed": false, "values_passed": 0, "values_total": 1, "expected_answer": 0.22330097087378642, "extracted_values": [0.186], "errors": ["Expected 0.22330097087378642, got 0.186"], "duration_seconds": 2.17478346824646, "prompt_tokens": 127, "completion_tokens": 101, "response_text": "The total number of balls in the box is 13 + 10 (red + yellow) + 80 (white). This gives a total of 123 balls.\n\nThe number of non-white balls are 13 (red) + 10 (yellow), which adds up to 23.\n\nSo, the probability that the drawn ball is not white is 23 out of 123 or approximately 0.186.\n"}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-12T09:38:00.963680", "model": "deepseek-coder:6.7b-instruct", "task_id": "math_006_6", "base_task_id": "math_006", "category_id": "6", "difficulty": "medium", "source_task_id": "6", "source_old_id": "vietjack_math_v5_0006", "passed": false, "values_passed": 0, "values_total": 1, "expected_answer": 0.22330097087378642, "extracted_values": [], "errors": ["Expected 1 numeric value(s), extracted 0: []"], "duration_seconds": 5.001863241195679, "prompt_tokens": 140, "completion_tokens": 253, "response_text": "The total number of balls in the box is the sum of all the balls i.e., 13 + 10 + 80 = 103.\n\nThe number of non-white balls are the red and yellow balls, so we add these two numbers together to get a total of 23 (13+10).\n\nSo, the probability that the drawn ball is not white is calculated as follows:\n\nP(not white) = 23/103\n\nThis can be computed in Python using the following code snippet:\n\n```python\ntotal_balls = 13 + 10 + 80  # Total number of balls\nwhite_balls = 80            # Number of white balls\nnon_white_balls = total_balls - white_balls   # Subtract the number of white balls from total to get non-white balls\nprobability_not_white = non_white_balls / total_balls  # Calculate probability\nprint(probability_not_white)\n```\n\nWhen you run this code, it will print out the probability that a randomly drawn ball is not white.\n"}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-12T09:38:07.772167", "model": "deepseek-coder:6.7b-instruct", "task_id": "math_006_7", "base_task_id": "math_006", "category_id": "7", "difficulty": "medium", "source_task_id": "6", "source_old_id": "vietjack_math_v5_0006", "passed": false, "values_passed": 0, "values_total": 1, "expected_answer": 0.22330097087378642, "extracted_values": [0.15384615384615385], "errors": ["Expected 0.22330097087378642, got 0.15384615384615385"], "duration_seconds": 6.806757926940918, "prompt_tokens": 138, "completion_tokens": 349, "response_text": "The total number of balls in the box is 13 + 10 (red + yellow) + 80 (white). So there are 93 balls in total.\n\nIf we want to find out the probability of drawing a non-white ball, we subtract the probability of drawing a white ball from 1. The probability of drawing a white ball is 80/93 or about 0.8462 (rounded to two decimal places). Therefore, the probability of drawing a non-white ball is 1 - 0.8462 = approximately 0.1538, rounded to two decimal places.\n\nHere's how you can calculate it in Python:\n\n```python\n# Define the number of balls of each color\nred_balls = 13\nyellow_balls = 10\nwhite_balls = 80\n\n# Calculate total number of balls\ntotal_balls = red_balls + yellow_balls + white_balls\n\n# Calculate probability of drawing a white ball\nprobability_of_white = white_balls / total_balls\n\n# Subtract the probability of drawing a white ball from 1 to get non-white ball probability\nnon_white_probability = 1 - probability_of_white\n\nprint(f\"The probability that the drawn ball is not white is {non_white_probability}\")\n```\nThis will output: \"The probability that the drawn ball is not white is 0.15384615384615385\".\n"}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-12T09:38:11.268305", "model": "deepseek-coder:6.7b-instruct", "task_id": "math_006_8", "base_task_id": "math_006", "category_id": "8", "difficulty": "medium", "source_task_id": "6", "source_old_id": "vietjack_math_v5_0006", "passed": false, "values_passed": 0, "values_total": 1, "expected_answer": 0.22330097087378642, "extracted_values": [0.235], "errors": ["Expected 0.22330097087378642, got 0.235"], "duration_seconds": 3.4947783946990967, "prompt_tokens": 154, "completion_tokens": 170, "response_text": "The total number of balls in the box is the sum of all the balls i.e., 13 + 10 + 80 = 103.\nSo, the probability that a non-white ball is drawn can be calculated by subtracting the probability of drawing a white ball from 1 (since the complementary event is drawing a white ball).\nThe total number of balls in the box are 103. The probability of drawing a white ball is 80/103 or approximately 0.765. Therefore, the probability that a non-white ball is drawn can be calculated as 1 - 0.765 = 0.235.\nSo, the answer to your question is approximately 0.235 or 23.5%.\n"}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-12T09:38:15.379217", "model": "deepseek-coder:6.7b-instruct", "task_id": "math_006_9", "base_task_id": "math_006", "category_id": "9", "difficulty": "medium", "source_task_id": "6", "source_old_id": "vietjack_math_v5_0006", "passed": false, "values_passed": 0, "values_total": 1, "expected_answer": 0.22330097087378642, "extracted_values": [0.6667000000000001], "errors": ["Expected 0.22330097087378642, got 0.6667000000000001"], "duration_seconds": 4.109288692474365, "prompt_tokens": 166, "completion_tokens": 201, "response_text": "The total number of balls in the box is the sum of all the balls i.e., 13 (red) + 10 (yellow) + 80 (white).\n\nSo, the probability that a ball drawn at random is not white can be calculated by subtracting the probability of drawing a white ball from 1. The probability of drawing any particular color ball is given as the number of balls in that color divided by the total number of balls. So, for red and yellow balls, their probabilities are 13/180 (for red) and 10/180 (for yellow).\n\nThe probability of not drawing a white ball can be calculated as follows:\n\nP(not white) = 1 - P(white)\n            = 1 - 80/180\n            = (120)/180.\n\nSo, the required probability is approximately 66.67%.\n"}
