{"timestamp": "2026-05-12T09:59:14.363135", "model": "deepseek-coder:6.7b-instruct", "task_id": "math_018_12", "base_task_id": "math_018", "category_id": "12", "difficulty": "easy", "source_task_id": "18", "source_old_id": "vietjack_math_v5_0018", "passed": false, "values_passed": 0, "values_total": 1, "expected_answer": 0.45454545454545453, "extracted_values": [2.0], "errors": ["Expected 0.45454545454545453, got 2.0"], "duration_seconds": 3.321486473083496, "prompt_tokens": 179, "completion_tokens": 160, "response_text": "The probability of an event can be calculated by dividing the number of favourable outcomes (outcomes where the event occurs) by the total number of possible outcomes. In this case, the favorable outcome is drawing a card that is a multiple of 2, and there are 5 such cards in the tray (2, 4, 6, 8, 10). The total number of possible outcomes is 11 (the total number of cards), so we can calculate the probability as follows:\n\nP(M) = 5 / 11\n\nThis gives us a probability of about 0.45, or 45%. So there's an 85% chance that the card drawn will be a multiple of 2.\n"}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-12T09:59:17.947186", "model": "deepseek-coder:6.7b-instruct", "task_id": "math_018_13", "base_task_id": "math_018", "category_id": "13", "difficulty": "easy", "source_task_id": "18", "source_old_id": "vietjack_math_v5_0018", "passed": false, "values_passed": 0, "values_total": 1, "expected_answer": 0.45454545454545453, "extracted_values": [2.0], "errors": ["Expected 0.45454545454545453, got 2.0"], "duration_seconds": 3.5825657844543457, "prompt_tokens": 182, "completion_tokens": 174, "response_text": "The probability of an event can be calculated by dividing the number of favourable outcomes (in this case, those where the number on the card is a multiple of 2) by the total number of possible outcomes (11 cards in all).\n\nHere's how you would calculate it using Python:\n\n```python\n# Total number of cards\ntotal_cards = 11\n\n# Number of favorable outcomes (multiples of 2)\nfavorable_outcomes = total_cards // 2\n\n# Calculate the probability\nprobability = favorable_outcomes / total_cards\nprint(probability)\n```\nThis program will output `0.5`, which is the probability that a randomly drawn card from the tray has a number that is a multiple of 2.\n"}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-12T09:59:23.018204", "model": "deepseek-coder:6.7b-instruct", "task_id": "math_018_14", "base_task_id": "math_018", "category_id": "14", "difficulty": "easy", "source_task_id": "18", "source_old_id": "vietjack_math_v5_0018", "passed": false, "values_passed": 0, "values_total": 1, "expected_answer": 0.45454545454545453, "extracted_values": [0.45], "errors": ["Expected 0.45454545454545453, got 0.45"], "duration_seconds": 5.069084882736206, "prompt_tokens": 197, "completion_tokens": 253, "response_text": "The probability of an event E (M in this case) can be calculated as follows: P(E) = Number of favorable outcomes / Total number of possible outcomes. In this scenario, we are looking for the probability that a randomly drawn card will have a number which is a multiple of 2. The numbers that meet this condition are {2,4,6,8,10}.\n\nSo, P(M) = 5 (the count of these numbers from 1 to 11) / 11 (total count of cards).\n\nLet's calculate it in Python:\n\n```python\n# Total number of cards\ntotal_cards = 11\n\n# Count of favorable outcomes\nfavorable_outcomes = total_cards // 2\n\n# Calculate the probability\nprobability = favorable_outcomes / total_cards\nprint(probability)\n```\nThis will output `0.4545`, which is the decimal equivalent of 45.45%. Thus, the probability that a randomly drawn card from the tray will have an even number on it is approximately 45.45% or 45%.\n"}
{"timestamp": "2026-05-12T09:59:27.617560", "model": "deepseek-coder:6.7b-instruct", "task_id": "math_018_15", "base_task_id": "math_018", "category_id": "15", "difficulty": "easy", "source_task_id": "18", "source_old_id": "vietjack_math_v5_0018", "passed": false, "values_passed": 0, "values_total": 1, "expected_answer": 0.45454545454545453, "extracted_values": [0.4], "errors": ["Expected 0.45454545454545453, got 0.4"], "duration_seconds": 4.597337961196899, "prompt_tokens": 210, "completion_tokens": 224, "response_text": "The probability of an event can be calculated by dividing the number of favourable outcomes (in this case, those where the drawn card is even) by the total number of possible outcomes (11 in this case). \n\nHere's a simple Python program to calculate it:\n\n```python\n# Total cards\ntotal_cards = 11\n\n# Cards that are multiples of 2\neven_numbers = [2, 4, 6, 8, 10]\nmultiples_of_two = len(even_numbers)\n\n# Calculate the probability\nprobability_M = multiples_of_two / total_cards\nprint(\"The probability of M is:\", probability_M)\n```\n\nWhen you run this program, it will output `0.4545` which is approximately equal to 2/5 or about `0.4`. So the probability that a randomly drawn card from the tray has an even number on it is around 40%.\n"}
